{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782086690540,"sessionID":"ses_1135b5c4dffe1dMwyYjBsXJ2H8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-93c66c5fc7d3df44","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node --version && npm --version && which npx","description":"Check node/npm versions"},"output":"v22.22.3\n10.9.8\n/Users/maui/.local/bin/npx\n","metadata":{"output":"v22.22.3\n10.9.8\n/Users/maui/.local/bin/npx\n","exit":0,"description":"Check node/npm versions","truncated":false},"title":"Check node/npm versions","time":{"start":1782086690537,"end":1782086690539}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a good understanding. Let me plan the implementation.\n\nI'll build a TypeScript MCP server for Brazilian soccer data. Let me set up:\n\n1. `package.json` with TypeScript, MCP SDK, CSV parser, test runner\n2. `tsconfig.json`\n3. Source files:\n   - `src/data/loader.ts` - CSV loading\n   - `src/data/normalizer.ts` - team name normalization, date parsing\n   - `src/query/engine.ts` - query functions (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)\n   - `src/mcp/server.ts` - MCP server exposing tools\n   - `src/index.ts` - entry point\n4. Tests using BDD-style (Jest or Vitest with given/when/then)\n\nLet me check what's available. The stack.json says framework \"unknown\", tooling \"none\". So I need to choose.\n\nLet me set up the project. I'll use:\n- TypeScript\n- @modelcontextprotocol/sdk\n- papaparse for CSV\n- vitest for tests (lightweight, BDD-style with describe/it)\n\nLet me check if node/npm is available.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eeca4e5ee00181okDlycKsXEct","sessionID":"ses_1135b5c4dffe1dMwyYjBsXJ2H8","messageID":"msg_eeca4d901001yrK2w1C7cVOq7m"}}
