{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088769752,"sessionID":"ses_1135b5c4dffe1dMwyYjBsXJ2H8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_9d3563a0f9694c7ca2cefe62","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md","newString":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n- License: Apache 2.0\n- data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv\n\n## Implementation\n\nA TypeScript MCP (Model Context Protocol) server exposing a knowledge-graph\ninterface over the datasets above. Implemented per `TASK.md` /\n`brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md`.\n\n### Stack\n- TypeScript (NodeNext ESM), strict mode\n- `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` for the MCP server (stdio transport)\n- `papaparse` for CSV parsing\n- `zod` for tool argument schemas\n- `vitest` for BDD-style tests (Given/When/Then)\n\n### Project layout\n```\nsrc/\n  types.ts       # domain types (Match, Player, TeamRecord, ...)\n  normalize.ts   # team-name & date normalization, TeamNameRegistry\n  loader.ts      # two-pass CSV loader (all 6 files) -> Dataset\n  query.ts       # query engine (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)\n  format.ts      # plain-text result formatters\n  server.ts      # MCP server + 13 registered tools\n  index.ts       # entry point (stdio)\ntest/\n  bdd.ts         # Given/When/Then helpers\n  fixtures.ts    # shared dataset loader\n  *.test.ts      # BDD specs for each capability category\n```\n\n### Build & test\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build        # tsc -> dist/\nnpm run typecheck    # tsc --noEmit (includes tests)\nnpm test             # vitest run\nnpm start            # node dist/index.js  (MCP over stdio)\n```\n\nThe data directory defaults to `./data/kaggle`; override with the\n`BR_SOCCER_DATA_DIR` environment variable.\n\n### MCP tools\n`search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `team_stats`, `search_players`,\n`top_players`, `standings`, `champion`, `relegated`, `competition_stats`,\n`biggest_wins`, `list_competitions`, `list_teams`, `list_seasons`.\n\n### Data-quality handling\n- **Team name variations**: a `TeamNameRegistry` scans the whole dataset and\n  keeps the `-UF` state suffix only when the base name is ambiguous (e.g.\n  `Atletico-MG` vs `Atletico-PR` are kept distinct, while `Palmeiras-SP`\n  normalizes to `Palmeiras`). Matching is accent- and case-insensitive with\n  substring fallback.\n- **Date formats**: ISO (`2023-09-24`), ISO+time (`2012-05-19 18:30:00`),\n  Brazilian (`29/03/2003`), and dotted (`2003.03.29`) are all parsed to\n  `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n- **Character encoding**: UTF-8 throughout (São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí).\n\n### Tests\n58 BDD specs across 8 files cover all five capability categories (match,\nteam, player, competition, statistical), the loader, normalization, and the\nMCP server tool layer (using an in-memory transport). The real Kaggle\ndatasets are loaded for the data-backed specs.\n","oldString":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n- License: Apache 2.0\n- data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md\n@@ -22,4 +22,68 @@\n \n https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n - License: Apache 2.0\n - data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv\n+\n+## Implementation\n+\n+A TypeScript MCP (Model Context Protocol) server exposing a knowledge-graph\n+interface over the datasets above. Implemented per `TASK.md` /\n+`brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md`.\n+\n+### Stack\n+- TypeScript (NodeNext ESM), strict mode\n+- `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` for the MCP server (stdio transport)\n+- `papaparse` for CSV parsing\n+- `zod` for tool argument schemas\n+- `vitest` for BDD-style tests (Given/When/Then)\n+\n+### Project layout\n+```\n+src/\n+  types.ts       # domain types (Match, Player, TeamRecord, ...)\n+  normalize.ts   # team-name & date normalization, TeamNameRegistry\n+  loader.ts      # two-pass CSV loader (all 6 files) -> Dataset\n+  query.ts       # query engine (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)\n+  format.ts      # plain-text result formatters\n+  server.ts      # MCP server + 13 registered tools\n+  index.ts       # entry point (stdio)\n+test/\n+  bdd.ts         # Given/When/Then helpers\n+  fixtures.ts    # shared dataset loader\n+  *.test.ts      # BDD specs for each capability category\n+```\n+\n+### Build & test\n+```bash\n+npm install\n+npm run build        # tsc -> dist/\n+npm run typecheck    # tsc --noEmit (includes tests)\n+npm test             # vitest run\n+npm start            # node dist/index.js  (MCP over stdio)\n+```\n+\n+The data directory defaults to `./data/kaggle`; override with the\n+`BR_SOCCER_DATA_DIR` environment variable.\n+\n+### MCP tools\n+`search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `team_stats`, `search_players`,\n+`top_players`, `standings`, `champion`, `relegated`, `competition_stats`,\n+`biggest_wins`, `list_competitions`, `list_teams`, `list_seasons`.\n+\n+### Data-quality handling\n+- **Team name variations**: a `TeamNameRegistry` scans the whole dataset and\n+  keeps the `-UF` state suffix only when the base name is ambiguous (e.g.\n+  `Atletico-MG` vs `Atletico-PR` are kept distinct, while `Palmeiras-SP`\n+  normalizes to `Palmeiras`). Matching is accent- and case-insensitive with\n+  substring fallback.\n+- **Date formats**: ISO (`2023-09-24`), ISO+time (`2012-05-19 18:30:00`),\n+  Brazilian (`29/03/2003`), and dotted (`2003.03.29`) are all parsed to\n+  `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n+- **Character encoding**: UTF-8 throughout (São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí).\n+\n+### Tests\n+58 BDD specs across 8 files cover all five capability categories (match,\n+team, player, competition, statistical), the loader, normalization, and the\n+MCP server tool layer (using an in-memory transport). The real Kaggle\n+datasets are loaded for the data-backed specs.\n+\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-e69ugumc/retort-7918d3908580/README.md\n@@ -22,4 +22,68 @@\n \n https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n - License: Apache 2.0\n - data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv\n+\n+## Implementation\n+\n+A TypeScript MCP (Model Context Protocol) server exposing a knowledge-graph\n+interface over the datasets above. Implemented per `TASK.md` /\n+`brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md`.\n+\n+### Stack\n+- TypeScript (NodeNext ESM), strict mode\n+- `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` for the MCP server (stdio transport)\n+- `papaparse` for CSV parsing\n+- `zod` for tool argument schemas\n+- `vitest` for BDD-style tests (Given/When/Then)\n+\n+### Project layout\n+```\n+src/\n+  types.ts       # domain types (Match, Player, TeamRecord, ...)\n+  normalize.ts   # team-name & date normalization, TeamNameRegistry\n+  loader.ts      # two-pass CSV loader (all 6 files) -> Dataset\n+  query.ts       # query engine (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)\n+  format.ts      # plain-text result formatters\n+  server.ts      # MCP server + 13 registered tools\n+  index.ts       # entry point (stdio)\n+test/\n+  bdd.ts         # Given/When/Then helpers\n+  fixtures.ts    # shared dataset loader\n+  *.test.ts      # BDD specs for each capability category\n+```\n+\n+### Build & test\n+```bash\n+npm install\n+npm run build        # tsc -> dist/\n+npm run typecheck    # tsc --noEmit (includes tests)\n+npm test             # vitest run\n+npm start            # node dist/index.js  (MCP over stdio)\n+```\n+\n+The data directory defaults to `./data/kaggle`; override with the\n+`BR_SOCCER_DATA_DIR` environment variable.\n+\n+### MCP tools\n+`search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `team_stats`, `search_players`,\n+`top_players`, `standings`, `champion`, `relegated`, `competition_stats`,\n+`biggest_wins`, `list_competitions`, `list_teams`, `list_seasons`.\n+\n+### Data-quality handling\n+- **Team name variations**: a `TeamNameRegistry` scans the whole dataset and\n+  keeps the `-UF` state suffix only when the base name is ambiguous (e.g.\n+  `Atletico-MG` vs `Atletico-PR` are kept distinct, while `Palmeiras-SP`\n+  normalizes to `Palmeiras`). Matching is accent- and case-insensitive with\n+  substring fallback.\n+- **Date formats**: ISO (`2023-09-24`), ISO+time (`2012-05-19 18:30:00`),\n+  Brazilian (`29/03/2003`), and dotted (`2003.03.29`) are all parsed to\n+  `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n+- **Character encoding**: UTF-8 throughout (São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí).\n+\n+### Tests\n+58 BDD specs across 8 files cover all five capability categories (match,\n+team, player, competition, statistical), the loader, normalization, and the\n+MCP server tool layer (using an in-memory transport). The real Kaggle\n+datasets are loaded for the data-backed specs.\n+\n","additions":64,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1782088769747,"end":1782088769750}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_eecc4a0ba001EfY5IjMQT25wWu","sessionID":"ses_1135b5c4dffe1dMwyYjBsXJ2H8","messageID":"msg_eecc45f23001O6MBP1qonG3TNE"}}
