{"type":"text","timestamp":1782088784987,"sessionID":"ses_1135b5c4dffe1dMwyYjBsXJ2H8","part":{"id":"prt_eecc4cedc001PcYZJ17N4b8ZF5","messageID":"msg_eecc4b96c001xw0XJvyVjkES8O","sessionID":"ses_1135b5c4dffe1dMwyYjBsXJ2H8","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server in TypeScript per `TASK.md`.\n\n**Summary**\n- **Source** (`src/`): `types.ts`, `normalize.ts` (team/date normalization + `TeamNameRegistry`), `loader.ts` (two-pass CSV loader for all 6 files), `query.ts` (match/team/player/competition/stats), `format.ts` (text formatters), `server.ts` (MCP server, 13 tools), `index.ts` (stdio entry).\n- **Tests** (`test/`): BDD Given/When/Then specs across 8 files — 58 tests, all passing.\n- **Verification**: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean, `npm test` → 58 passed, and a stdio smoke test confirmed the server lists 13 tools and answers `champion` (Flamengo 2019, 90 pts) and `head_to_head` queries.\n\n**Notable correctness fix:** the state-suffix normalizer keeps `-MG`/`-PR`/`-GO` for ambiguous base names (so Atlético-MG and Atlético-PR stay distinct), which makes the computed 2019 Brasileirão champion come out as Flamengo with 90 pts — matching the spec's example output exactly.\n\nOne quirk worth flagging: vitest 4 reserves the lowercase `given`/`when`/`then` identifiers (native BDD collector), so the BDD helpers use capitalized `Given`/`When`/`Then`.","time":{"start":1782088781532,"end":1782088784983}}}
